# Quality Rule

A feature is not complete until it is tested.

Required checks before final delivery:

- TypeScript passes with no ignored errors.
- Lint passes.
- Unit tests pass.
- Production build passes.
- Playwright route and form tests pass.
- Axe checks show no serious or critical violations.
- Key routes render at 1440px, 1024px, and 390px widths.
- No console errors or hydration warnings.
- No horizontal overflow.
- Keyboard navigation and visible focus work.
- Reduced-motion mode remains complete and understandable.
- Forms show success, invalid, server-error, and rate-limit states.
- All internal links resolve.
- Staging is noindex; production is indexable as specified.
- Metadata, sitemap, robots, canonical, and JSON-LD are inspected in the rendered HTML.

Do not suppress a failing test merely to complete the build.
